    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d316">

                <pb facs="0322" n="1000" xml:id="pg1000"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Motley</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 30.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-02-26"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >February</hi> 26, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Your very interesting despatch of January
                    21 (No. 17) has been received. The survey of continental politics which you have
                    taken in this paper is full of instruction. If questions purely dynastic, or of
                    mere administration, or, at most, of political organization, can make and keep
                    so many European nations so unquiet, as to require constant vigilance on the
                    part of their governments, one would expect that they could afford to be
                    tolerant of this government, in its efforts to preserve, in its full efficiency,
                    a system that is so perfect as to be undisturbed by questions of those sorts,
                    and encounters an opposition or resistance from only one disturbing cause, and
                    that one African slavery, which the public sentiment of mankind elsewhere
                    unanimously condemns.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>J. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lothrop Motley</hi>, Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., Vienna.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
